===Etymology===
{{confix|en|rhabdo|mancy}}, first attested in 1646. From {{bor|en|la|rhabdomantīa}}, from {{der|en|grc|ῥαβδομαντεία}}, from {{m|grc|ῥάβδος||rod}} + {{m|grc|μαντεία||divination}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɹæb.dəˌmæn.si/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-rhabdomancy.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# [[divination|Divination]] with [[wand]]s or [[rod]]s, especially to use a [[divining rod]] to find things below the ground.
#: {{syn|en|dowsing}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1936|author=Rollo Ahmed|title=The Black Art|publisher=Long|location=London|page=145|passage=This question of buried treasure exercised the minds of ancient occultists considerably, and in connection with it there was frequently employed the art of '''Rhabdomancy''', which was similar to that of water divining or water "dousing".}}

